// spec ch05 §5.12: the closure holds a reborrow derived from `r` for as
// long as it lives, so `r` must keep its own borrow of `x` alive that
// whole time -- a lender's *name* going dead does not end the borrow
// once something derived from it is still outstanding. Writing `x`
// underneath the closure is therefore rejected.
int main() {
    int x = 7;
    int& r = x;
    auto i = [&r]() { return r; };
    x = 9;
    return i();
}
